  <data name="HomePage_WelcomeTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Welcome to Live Photo Box</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Intro1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A photo captures a moment. A Live Photo captures the moments before and after it.

But when you switch phones, move to a new computer, or transfer your photos from one platform to another, those once-living moments can easily stop moving simply because the devices handle them differently. Live Photo Box is built to bring those memories back to life.

Whether your Live Photos come from Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, vivo, Huawei, HONOR, Samsung, Google, or other devices, you can merge, split, convert, repair, and edit them all in one place. Live Photo Box goes beyond simply making a photo "move." It preserves as much of the original experience as possible — including HDR, EXIF data, capture time, camera settings, and other original image and video information. When you move your photos across devices and platforms, you are not just carrying over a moving picture, but also the details and character that made that memory yours.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Intro2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In "Merge &amp; Split", you can freely convert between different manufacturers' Live Photo formats, combine an image and a video into a Live Photo, or extract the original photo and video from an existing one. In "Edit", you can choose a new cover frame, adjust the moving content, and export your edited Live Photo in another format, giving the same memory a new way to live on. For common Apple Live Photo issues such as incorrect orientation and stretched images, "Repair" also provides dedicated fixes.

Live Photo Box is about more than handling one type of photo. It is about giving Live Photos from different brands the freedom to move across devices and platforms — so they can be saved, shared, and experienced the way they were meant to be.

Devices change. Platforms change. But the memories that belong to you shouldn't have to lose their life.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_TipLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tip :</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_TipText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Before using merge or split features, make sure you have backups of the original files. Data safety comes first.</value>
  </data>
