  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step01_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>📁 Set Input &amp; Output</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step01_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Prepare your source files and choose where the merged photos will be saved.

**📥 Input directory:** Pick a folder with images and videos. The app will scan and pair them automatically (this replaces the entire task queue). The input directory is not required — any content in the queue works.

**📤 Output directory:** Where the merged Live Photos will be saved.

**🔍 Scan button:** Scanning starts automatically once you set the input directory. You can also click "Scan" to refresh manually.

**⚙️ Scanning method:** Sub‑folders are not scanned by default. Go to "Settings" → "General" to enable **Scan Subfolders**.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step02_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🖱️ Drag &amp; Drop</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step02_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You can also drag and drop files and folders directly.

**📂 Folders:** Dragging to the left panel replaces the entire queue (clears it first, then adds the new content). Dragging to the right panel appends them.

**📄 Files:** Dragging individual files always appends to the queue without replacing anything.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step03_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🔗 Matching Method</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step03_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Determines how photos and videos are paired together.

**👍** The default filename-based matching is fine for most cases.

**⚠️** Switch only when you have files from multiple devices and want to filter for a specific protocol.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step04_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>📱 Protocol</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step04_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Determines which devices can recognize the Live Photo format.

**📋** Each protocol has a detailed description in the dropdown list.

**🖥️** If you only need to view on Windows, Google V2 is recommended.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step05_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>📦 Output Format</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step05_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose the format combination for the output files.

**🎯** Pick the one that suits your needs. The first option is generally a good starting point.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step06_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🏷️ Naming Template</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step06_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Customize how output files are named.

**📋** Use built-in presets or add your own segments.

**🔀** Drag each segment to reorder.

**👁️** A live preview shows the final filename below.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step07_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🚀 Start Merging</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MergeTutorial_Step07_Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Once you have confirmed the input/output directories and the task queue, you are ready to start.

**✅** Click "Start Merge" to begin processing all tasks with your settings.</value>
  </data>
