  <data name="HomePage_Tutorial_Step1_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Place your Live Photos (photo + video) in the same folder. File names must match; only the extension differs.

Supported image formats: JPG/JPEG, HEIC/HEIF
Supported video formats: MOV, MP4

✅ IMG_001.JPG + IMG_001.MOV
❌ IMG_001.JPG + VID_001.MOV</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Tutorial_Step2_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On the "Live Photo Merge" page, click the "Browse" button and select the folder you just prepared. The output directory is set automatically by default; change it only if you need a custom location.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Tutorial_Step3_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>After scanning, pick a protocol in the "Merge Protocol" dropdown, then choose the output format:

· Google Micro Video (v1)
· Google Motion Photo (v2)
· OPPO O-Live Photo
· HUAWEI Moving Photo

· vivo Live Photo (≥ x300) ⚠️ In testing
· Samsung Motion Photo ⚠️ In testing

💡 For supported devices, see the hint in the "Merge Protocol" dropdown

Output format (image + video):
· JPEG + MP4 — Universal, best compatibility
· JPEG + MOV — Apple style
· HEIC + MP4 / HEIC + MOV — Smaller size
· HEIC + MP4 (H.265) — HUAWEI native only

Once selected, click "Start Merge".</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Tutorial_Step4_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The merging process runs automatically — no extra action needed. Once done, the output folder contains your merged Live Photos!

The resulting single-file format can be viewed and played directly on both Windows and Android devices ~</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_SplitTutorial_Step1_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Single-file Live Photos (one file holding both the still image and the motion video) support these protocols:

· Google Micro Video (v1)
· Google Motion Photo (v2)
· OPPO O-Live Photo
· HUAWEI Moving Photo

· vivo Live Photo ⚠️ In testing
· Samsung Motion Photo ⚠️ In testing

💡 For supported devices, see the hint in the "Match" dropdown

Pick the matching protocol type or "All single-file Live Photo" and place the files in one folder.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_SplitTutorial_Step2_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Click "Browse" to choose a folder; the app scans and recognizes Live Photos automatically. After verifying the stats, pick the output protocol &amp; format:

· None — export the photo + video as-is
· Apple — JPG + MOV / HEIC + MOV
· vivo (≤ x200) — JPG + MP4 ⚠️ In testing

Then click "Start Split".</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_SplitTutorial_Step3_Desc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Once splitting is complete, you will find photo and video files with matching file names in the output folder. Simply open them to review.</value>
  </data>
